WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Controls and thermostats are the brain of the system. When they fail, nothing
works right.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Three charging methods: Subcooling method for TXV systems — measure liquid line
pressure, convert to saturation temp, measure actual liquid line temp,
subcooling equals saturation minus actual. Target is typically 10-15F per

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Subcooling Method: Charging method for TXV systems. Target typically 10-15F.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Weigh-In Method: Add exact nameplate charge by weight after complete evacuation.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Using the wrong charging method is one of
the most common technician errors. It leads to overcharge or undercharge and
callbacks.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: TXV = subcooling method. And — Piston = superheat method
with charging chart

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

